            <ArticleTitle>Lornoxicam-induced hair loss: an unusual case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>218-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/0022-3859.118042</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient started on 8 mg lornoxicam twice daily for pain in the hips developed acute-onset scalp hair loss. History and clinical examination revealed no evident abnormalities. Temporal association of the onset of hair loss with the use of lornoxicam, inability to explain hair loss by alternate causes, possibility of hair loss with lornoxicam and resolution on dechallenge placed this reaction as a probable adverse reaction to lornoxicam.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
